sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant K8s as Kubernetes Ingress/Proxy<br/>Authentication Layer
    participant Server as NeMo-Guardrails FastAPI<br/>Port 8000
    participant InputR as Input Rails<br/>Jailbreak/Content/Prompt
    participant HeaderFwd as Header Forwarding<br/>Module
    participant LLM as LLM Provider<br/>(OpenAI / Azure OpenAI)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OutputR as Output Rails<br/>Fact-Check/Moderation/PII
    participant GuardAPI as Third-Party Guardrail APIs<br/>(ActiveFence, AI Defense, etc.)

    Note over Client,GuardAPI: Inbound Request Flow

    Client->>K8s: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Authorization: Bearer <k8s-token><br/>X-Authorization: Bearer <llm-api-key>
    K8s->>Server: Authenticated request forwarded<br/>Headers preserved

    Server->>Server: Load guardrail config<br/>(YAML/Colang files)

    Note over Server,GuardAPI: Input Rail Processing

    Server->>InputR: Apply input rails
    InputR->>InputR: Jailbreak detection<br/>(heuristic checks)
    InputR->>InputR: Content filtering<br/>(spaCy NLP analysis)

    opt Third-party guardrail check
        InputR->>GuardAPI: Check content<br/>Auth: Provider API key (env var)
        GuardAPI-->>InputR: Allow/Deny result
    end

    alt Input rails REJECT
        InputR-->>Server: Blocked (policy violation)
        Server-->>K8s: 200 OK with guardrail response
        K8s-->>Client: Guardrail rejection message
    else Input rails PASS
        InputR-->>Server: Content approved

        Note over Server,LLM: LLM Provider Interaction

        Server->>HeaderFwd: Prepare outbound auth
        HeaderFwd->>HeaderFwd: Map X-Authorization → Authorization<br/>(exclude inbound Authorization header)

        HeaderFwd->>LLM: POST /chat/completions<br/>Authorization: Bearer <llm-api-key><br/>TLS 1.2+
        LLM-->>Server: LLM response

        Note over Server,GuardAPI: Output Rail Processing

        Server->>OutputR: Apply output rails
        OutputR->>OutputR: Fact-checking<br/>(AlignScore / NLI)
        OutputR->>OutputR: PII anonymization<br/>(Presidio)
        OutputR->>OutputR: Content moderation

        opt Third-party output check
            OutputR->>GuardAPI: Validate output<br/>Auth: Provider API key
            GuardAPI-->>OutputR: Allow/Modify result
        end

        OutputR-->>Server: Processed response
        Server-->>K8s: 200 OK with filtered response
        K8s-->>Client: JSON response
    end

    Note over Client,GuardAPI: Guardrail Check Flow (standalone)

    Client->>K8s: POST /v1/guardrail/checks<br/>role-based rail routing
    K8s->>Server: Forward request
    Server->>Server: Route by message role:<br/>user/system → input rails<br/>assistant → output rails<br/>tool → tool_input rails
    Server-->>K8s: Check result
    K8s-->>Client: Pass/Fail response
